#N canvas 120 60 1100 460 12;
#X text 20 10 fs_viz <name> <port> - forwards this sensor's sphere data to the sphere editor (python tools/sphere_edit.py \, listens on 12346): aim + sphere from the Pi's Alignment stage \, and gate from [fs_sphere] (how much the motion gate lets through). Inlet: 1 = on \, 0 = off (default off \, so nothing is sent when the editor isn't running). Sends to 127.0.0.1 as /fs/<name>/aim \, /fs/<name>/sphere \, /fs/<name>/gate., f 120;
#X obj 20 110 inlet;
#X obj 20 140 t f f;
#X obj 20 180 sel 0;
#X msg 20 220 disconnect;
#X obj 110 220 t b;
#X obj 110 250 f \$2;
#X msg 110 280 connect 127.0.0.1 \$1;
#X obj 20 380 netsend -u -b;
#X obj 400 110 fs_in \$1 aim;
#X obj 400 180 spigot;
#X obj 400 250 oscformat fs \$1 aim;
#X obj 620 110 fs_in \$1 sphere;
#X obj 620 180 spigot;
#X obj 620 250 oscformat fs \$1 sphere;
#X obj 840 110 fs_in \$1 gate;
#X obj 840 180 spigot;
#X obj 840 250 oscformat fs \$1 gate;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 2 0 3 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 3 1 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 7 0;
#X connect 4 0 8 0;
#X connect 7 0 8 0;
#X connect 2 1 10 1;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 10 0 11 0;
#X connect 11 0 8 0;
#X connect 2 1 13 1;
#X connect 12 0 13 0;
#X connect 13 0 14 0;
#X connect 14 0 8 0;
#X connect 2 1 16 1;
#X connect 15 0 16 0;
#X connect 16 0 17 0;
#X connect 17 0 8 0;
